<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Area of a region below the x-axis</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A drainage ditch on a farm in Nakuru has cross-section \(y = {@yx@}\) for \(0 \le x \le {@ww@}\), where \(x\) and \(y\) are in metres and \(y = 0\) is ground level.</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Cross-section of the ditch: a curve below the ground line y = 0 from x = 0 to x = {#ww#} metres, deepest at the middle, {#float(dep)#} metres below ground. The region between the curve and the ground line is shaded.">[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="240px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [{#bxl#}, {#byt#}, {#bxr#}, {#byb#}], axis: true, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  var w = {#ww#}, kq = {#float(kq)#}, d = {#float(dep)#};
  var f = function(x) { return kq * x * x - kq * w * x; };
  b.create('functiongraph', [f, 0, w], {strokeColor: '#003399', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  var pts = [], n = 60;
  for (var i = 0; i <= n; i++) { var xi = i * w / n; pts.push([xi, f(xi)]); }
  b.create('polygon', pts, {fillColor: '#8B5A2B', fillOpacity: 0.25, borders: {strokeWidth: 0}, vertices: {visible: false}, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('segment', [[w / 2, 0], [w / 2, -d]], {strokeColor: '#000000', dash: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('text', [w / 2 + 0.1, -d / 2, 'depth ' + d + ' m'], {anchorX: 'left', fixed: true, highlight: false});
  b.create('text', [w * 0.75, 0.3 * d, 'ground level, y = 0'], {anchorX: 'middle', fixed: true, highlight: false});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]</div><p>Give exact values.</p><p>(a) Find \(\displaystyle \int_0^{ {@ww@} } y\,dx\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the area of the cross-section of the ditch.</p><div>Area \(=\) [[input:ans2]] \(\text{m}^2\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) The ditch is \({@Ln@}\) m long. Find the volume of soil dug out.</p><div>Volume \(=\) [[input:ans3]] m\(^3\) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The ditch is below ground level, so \(y\) is negative for \(0 \lt x \lt {@ww@}\) and the integral is negative. The area is the size of the integral.</p><p>(a) \[\int_0^{ {@ww@} } \left({@yx@}\right)dx = \left[{@Yx@}\right]_0^{ {@ww@} } = {@I@}\]</p><p>(b) The area of the cross-section is \({@Ar@}\) \(\text{m}^2\).</p><p>(c) Volume \(=\) area of cross-section \(\times\) length \(= {@Ar@} \times {@Ln@} = {@Vol@}\) m\(^3\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: a negative integral. [w, k, length]; y = k x^2 - k w x below ground for 0 < x < w. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 11, section D, D1. */
L: [[6,1/8,20],[6,1/9,50],[6,1/12,25],[3,1/2,40],[3,1/3,30],[4,3/16,50],[5,6/25,20],[5,3/25,40],[2,3/4,100],[8,3/64,25]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
ww: L[ix][1]; kq: L[ix][2]; Ln: L[ix][3];
yx: kq*x^2-kq*ww*x;
Yx: integrate(yx,x);
I: subst(x=ww,Yx);
Ar: -I;
Vol: -I*Ln;
dep: kq*ww^2/4;
/* board */
bxl: -0.6; bxr: float(ww+0.6); byt: float(0.6*dep); byb: float(-1.4*dep);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
